    '### VIEW DEFINITION CONTROL VIEW DEFINITION

An application role is a database-level securable contained by the database that is its parent in
the permissions hierarchy. The most specific and limited permissions that can be granted on an
application role are listed in the following, together with the more general permissions that
include them by implication.
Application role
permission
Implied by application role
permission
Implied by database
