    '### GO

```

See Also



```sql
GRANT Database Scoped Credential
```

permissions (Transact-SQL)
Applies to:  SQL Server 2017 (14.x) and later versions  Azure SQL Database  Azure
SQL Managed Instance  Azure Synapse Analytics  SQL database in Microsoft Fabric
Grants permissions on a database scoped credential.
 Transact-SQL syntax conventions
syntaxsql
Specifies a permission that can be granted on a database scoped credential. Listed below.
Specifies the database scoped credential on which the permission is being granted. The scope
qualifier "::" is required.
Specifies the principal to which the permission is being granted. One of the following:
database user
database role
application role
database user mapped to a Windows login
database user mapped to a Windows group
database user mapped to a certificate
Syntax
```sql
GRANT permission  [ ,...n ]
```

    ON DATABASE SCOPED CREDENTIAL :: credential_name
    TO principal [ ,...n ] [ WITH GRANT OPTION ]
    [ AS granting_principal ]
Arguments
permission
ON DATABASE SCOPED CREDENTIAL ::credential_name
database_principal



database user mapped to an asymmetric key
database user not mapped to a server principal.
Indicates that the principal will also be given the ability to grant the specified permission to
other principals.
Specifies a principal from which the principal executing this query derives its right to grant the
permission. One of the following:
database user
database role
application role
database user mapped to a Windows login
database user mapped to a Windows group
database user mapped to a certificate
database user mapped to an asymmetric key
database user not mapped to a server principal.
A database scoped credential is a database-level securable contained by the database that is
its parent in the permissions hierarchy. The most specific and limited permissions that can be
granted on a database scoped credential are listed below, together with the more general
permissions that include them by implication.
Database scoped credential
permission
Implied by database scoped
credential permission
Implied by database
