    '### VIEW DEFINITION CONTROL VIEW DEFINITION

A Service Broker service is a database-level securable contained by the database that is its
parent in the permissions hierarchy. The most specific and limited permissions that can be
granted on a Service Broker service are listed below, together with the more general
permissions that include them by implication.
Service Broker service
permission
Implied by Service Broker service
permission
Implied by database
permission',
