VALUES (
    'chunk_e2c1ff91432d',
    'converted_sql-sql-server-ver17.md',
    55704,
    '### WITH GRANT OPTION

Indicates that the principal will also be given the ability to grant the specified permission to other
principals.
AS <database_principal> Specifies a principal from which the principal executing this query
derives its right to grant the permission.
Database_user
Specifies a database user.
Database_role
Specifies a database role.
Application_role
Specifies an application role.
Database_user_mapped_to_Windows_User
Specifies a database user mapped to a Windows user.
Database_user_mapped_to_Windows_Group
Specifies a database user mapped to a Windows group.
Database_user_mapped_to_certificate
Specifies a database user mapped to a certificate.
Database_user_mapped_to_asymmetric_key
Specifies a database user mapped to an asymmetric key.
Database_user_with_no_login
Specifies a database user with no corresponding server-level principal.
Information about symmetric keys is visible in the sys.symmetric_keys catalog view.
A symmetric key is a database-level securable contained by the database that is its parent in the
permissions hierarchy. The most specific and limited permissions that can be granted on a
Remarks



symmetric key are listed in the following table, together with the more general permissions that
include them by implication.
Symmetric key permission Implied by symmetric key permission Implied by database permission',
