    '### GO

See Also



```sql
GRANT XML Schema Collection
```

Permissions (Transact-SQL)
Article • 09/03/2024
Applies to:  SQL Server
Grants permissions on an XML schema collection.
 Transact-SQL syntax conventions
syntaxsql
permission
Specifies a permission that can be granted on an XML schema collection. For a list of the
permissions, see the Remarks section later in this topic.
ON XML SCHEMA COLLECTION :: [ schema_name. ] XML_schema_collection_name
Specifies the XML schema collection on which the permission is being granted. The scope
qualifier (::) is required. If schema_name is not specified, the default schema will be used. If
schema_name is specified, the schema scope qualifier (.) is required.
<database_principal> Specifies the principal to which the permission is being granted.
Syntax

```sql
GRANT permission  [ ,...n ] ON
```

