See Also



REVOKE Database Principal Permissions
(Transact-SQL)
Applies to:  SQL Server  Azure SQL Database  Azure SQL Managed Instance  SQL
database in Microsoft Fabric
Revokes permissions granted or denied on a database user, database role, or application role.
 Transact-SQL syntax conventions
syntaxsql
permission
Specifies a permission that can be revoked on the database principal. For a list of the
permissions, see the Remarks section later in this topic.
USER ::database_user
Specifies the class and name of the user on which the permission is being revoked. The scope
qualifier (::) is required.
