    '### VIEW DEFINITION CONTROL VIEW DEFINITION

A Service Broker service is a database-level securable that is contained by the database that is
its parent in the permissions hierarchy. The most specific and limited permissions that can be
revoked on a Service Broker service are listed in the following table, together with the more
general permissions that include them by implication.
Service Broker service
permission
Implied by Service Broker service
permission
Implied by database
permission',
