    56199,
    '### (PDW)

Revokes permissions granted or denied on an XML schema collection.
 Transact-SQL syntax conventions
syntaxsql
permission
Specifies a permission that can be revoked on an XML schema collection. For a list of the
permissions, see the Remarks section later in this topic.
ON XML SCHEMA COLLECTION :: [ schema_name. ] XML_schema_collection_name
Specifies the XML schema collection on which the permission is being revoked. The scope
qualifier (::) is required. If schema_name is not specified, the default schema will be used. If
schema_name is specified, the schema scope qualifier (.) is required.
Syntax
REVOKE [ GRANT OPTION FOR ] permission [ ,...n ] ON
    XML SCHEMA COLLECTION :: [ schema_name . ]
    XML_schema_collection_name
    { TO | FROM } <database_principal> [ ,...n ]',
