    'converted_sql-sql-server-ver17.md',
    56456,
    '### SQL

The results are show in the following table.
EqualNull DifferentNull EqualZero DifferentZero
True False False True
With SET ANSI_NULLS ON  all expressions would be evaluated as ''False'' because NULL  cannot be
compared with NULL  or 0  using these operators.
The following example uses the Equals (= ) and Not Equal To (<> ) comparison operators to make
comparisons with NULL  and non-null values in a table. The example also shows the SET
ANSI_NULLS  setting does not affect IS NULL .',
