comparisons. Also, SQL Server uses the same casting rules for untyped values during value
comparisons as it uses during general comparisons. In contrast, the rules in the XQuery
specification always cast the untyped value to xs:string during value comparisons.
The node comparison operator, is, applies only to node types. The result it returns indicates
whether two nodes passed in as operands represent the same node in the source document. This
operator returns True if the two operands are the same node. Otherwise, it returns False.
