    57204,
    '### SQL

The computed element and attribute constructors, as defined in the XQuery specification, allow
you to compute the node names. When you''re using direct constructors in SQL Server, the
node names, such as element and attribute, must be specified as constant literals. Therefore,
there''s no difference in the direct constructors and computed constructors for elements and
attributes.
In the following example, the content for the constructed nodes is obtained from the XML
manufacturing instructions stored in the Instructions column of the xml data type in the
ProductModel table.',
