INSERT INTO document_chunks (id, source_file, chunk_index, content, metadata, embedding)
VALUES (
    'chunk_f4139a0bba49',
    'converted_sql-sql-server-ver17.md',
    57300,
    '### SQL

In the previous query, the exist()  method of the xml data type in the WHERE  clause checks to
see if there''s a <Weight>  element in the <Specifications>  element.
The XML product catalog description includes the product pictures, the <Picture>  element.
Each picture has several properties, including the picture angle (the <Angle>  element), and the
size (the <Size>  element).
<Product ProductModelID="19"/>
<Product ProductModelID="23"/>
<Product ProductModelID="25"/>
<Product ProductModelID="28"><Weight>Varies with size.</Weight></Product>
<Product ProductModelID="34"/>
<Product ProductModelID="35"/>
WITH XMLNAMESPACES (''https://schemas.microsoft.com/sqlserver/2004/07/adventure-
works/ProductModelDescription'' AS pd)
```sql
SELECT CatalogDescription.query(''
```

          <Product  ProductModelID="{ (/pd:ProductDescription/@ProductModelID)[1]
}">
                 {
                      /pd:ProductDescription/pd:Specifications/Weight
                 }
          </Product>
'') AS x
FROM Production.ProductModel
WHERE CatalogDescription.exist(''/pd:ProductDescription/pd:Specifications//Weight
'') = 1;
B. Find product model IDs for product models whose catalog
descriptions include front-angle and small size pictures



For product models whose catalog descriptions include front-angle and small-size pictures, the
query constructs XML that has the following form:',
