    'chunk_231af1d25572',
    'converted_sql-sql-server-ver17.md',
    57304,
    '### XML

</p1:Product>
...
C. Create a flat list of the product model name and feature
pairs, with each pair enclosed in the <Features> element
```sql
SELECT CatalogDescription.query(''
```

declare namespace p1="https://schemas.microsoft.com/sqlserver/2004/07/adventure-
works/ProductModelDescription";
  for $pd in /p1:ProductDescription,
   $f in $pd/p1:Features/*
  return
   <Feature>
     <ProductModelName> { data($pd/@ProductModelName) } </ProductModelName>
     { $f }
  </Feature>
'') AS x
FROM Production.ProductModel
WHERE ProductModelID = 19;
<Feature>
 <ProductModelName>Mountain 100</ProductModelName>
 <ProductModelID>19</ProductModelID>
 <p1:Warranty



Using the information stored in the catalog description of the product model, the following
query lists the product model name, model ID, and features grouped inside a <Product>
element.',
