    57310,
    '### SQL

The SELECT  query specifies query()  and value()  methods of the xml data type. Therefore,
instead of repeating the namespaces declaration two times in two difference query prologs,
the prefix pd  is used in the query and is defined only once by using WITH XMLNAMESPACES .
Note the following considerations from the previous query:
The WHERE  clause is used to retrieve only the rows where the catalog description contains
the word "Aerodynamic" in the <Summary>  element.
The contains()  function is used to see if the word is included in the text.
The value()  method of the xml data type compares the value returned by contains()  to
1.
Here''s the result:',
